  "rules": {
    "S": "S(arm) = #cells where the donor-new-source patch is JOINT and the donor-ROUND-source patch of the same arm is not (target host new)",
    "SPEC": "SPEC iff dM_main > dM_round in >= 75% of cells AND in a majority of cells for >= 10 of 14 donor groups",
    "SUF": "SUF(arm) iff S(arm) >= 1/2 S(full) and SPEC(arm)",
    "always_reported": "S, SPEC, J_main, J_round and median dM per arm; per host; leave-one-donor-group-out of every verdict; energy, alpha and capped share of the subspace arms; change norm of every arm relative to the full patch; all nulls",
    "consistency_gate": "full = the M3 all-heads patch: its 208 rows equal M3's bitwise and S(full) = 51; meanD_host = the M6 pooled-donor arm: its 208 rows equal M6's bitwise and S = 39 (GPU, checked in the run); otherwise every verdict is INCONSISTENT_WITH_M3_M6 and no claim",
    "delta_lowrank_verdict": "k* = the smallest k in 1, 4, 16, 64 with SUF(dlr{k}_sm); NULL holds iff S(rand64_sm) <= 5 and not SPEC(rand64_sm). DELTA_LOWRANK:k* if k* exists and NULL holds; DELTA_LOWRANK_UNRESOLVED:k* if k* exists and NULL fails; NOT_DELTA_LOWRANK_LE64 if no k*",
    "interpretation_fixed_in_advance": "DELTA_LOWRANK:k: the repairing part of the cell's donor-minus-host BULK difference lies in a k-dimensional subspace of OTHER donors' differences to the same host, at matched size, and a random subspace at that size does not repair. NOT_DELTA_LOWRANK_LE64: not even a 64-dimensional difference subspace carries it. LR64_SIZE_LIMITED: M6's lr64 failure (S 10) was a size effect of the unrescaled projection; LR64_BASIS_LIMITED: it was the raw basis. MEANDIFF_DIRECTION:s: one fixed position-wise vector per source kind, the pooled donor BULK minus the pooled host BULK, added to the host repairs it round-specifically: the shared component is a donor-vs-host difference, not the donor's absolute BULK. RC_GENERIC: the new-vs-ROUND contrast of other hosts' BULK alone, subtracted (main) or added (round), produces the round-specific JOINT pattern: the round contrast needs no repairing donor. RC_DONOR_POOL_ONLY: only the donors' contrast does. RC_INSUFFICIENT: the contrast alone is not enough. The mdir and rc arms vary with the donor only through the pool exclusion (effectively 8 hosts); per-host S is the honest unit there. The mdir and rc arms are not size-matched; their change norms relative to full are reported. A rescaled arm at large alpha (capped at 10) is off-distribution; alpha and the capped share are reported",
    "m6_lr64_size": "LR64_SIZE_LIMITED if SUF(lr64_sm), else LR64_BASIS_LIMITED",
    "meandiff_verdict": "s* = the smallest s in 1, 2 with SUF(mdir{s}); MEANDIFF_DIRECTION:s* if s* exists and NULL holds; MEANDIFF_UNRESOLVED:s* if s* exists and NULL fails; NOT_MEANDIFF otherwise",
    "readouts": "M = conflict margin; A = logit(reject_conflict) - max(accept, wait); JOINT = M > 0 and A > 0; dM = M(patch) - M(in-run capture of host new)",
    "round_contrast_verdict": "RC_GENERIC if SUF(rcH); RC_DONOR_POOL_ONLY if SUF(rcD) and not SUF(rcH); RC_INSUFFICIENT otherwise; the median dM of the round source (+contrast) and of the main source (-contrast) of rcH and rcD are always reported",
    "size_gate": "per row and span position, the change of a rescaled arm equals min(||delta_B||, 10 ||U_k U_k^T delta_B||) (dlr*_sm, lr64_sm) or ||delta_B|| (rand64_sm) within 1e-3 relative (fail-closed in the runner); energy ||U_k U_k^T delta_B|| / ||delta_B||, alpha and the capped share are recorded",
    "units": "the 104 cross-group cells of M1-M6; cells share donors and hosts, and the pooled-mean arms vary with the donor only through the pool exclusion (effectively 8 hosts), so counts are descriptive decision rules, not independent tests; per-host S is always reported"
  },
